{"name":"Cerulean","hex":"#55aaee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cerulean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A greenish-blue color.","Any of various lycaenid butterflies of the genus Jamides."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sky-blue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cerulean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cerulean","blocks":[{"text":"The color cerulean, or caerulean, is a variety of the hue of blue that may range from a light azure blue to a more intense sky blue. Cerulean may also be mixed with the hue of green. The first recorded use of cerulean as a color name in English was in 1590. The word is derived from the Latin word caeruleus, \"dark blue, blue, or blue-green\", which in turn probably derives from caerulum, diminutive of caelum, \"heaven, sky\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerulean","wikidata":"Q313120"},{"title":"Cerulean (Baths album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cerulean is the debut studio album by American electronic musician Baths. It was released on June 22, 2010, by Anticon."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5d/BathsCeruleanCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerulean_(Baths_album)","wikidata":"Q5065292"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/250px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/500px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG/250px-PB35_Bleu_C%C3%A9rul%C3%A9um.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3